.TH DAILYDECK 1 "2026-11-03" "dailydeck 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dailydeck \- Stream Deck shows the keyboard shortcuts of the focused window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dailydeck
[\fB\-c\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-v\fR]
[\fB\-\-tray\fR | \fB\-\-gui\fR | \fB\-\-print\-focus\fR | \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR \fISHORTCUT\fR | \fB\-\-preview\fR \fIDIR\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dailydeck
switches an Elgato Stream Deck to the profile of the application that has the focus and
sends the configured shortcut when a key is pressed.
Without a mode option it runs as a daemon without user interface.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Configuration file (default: \fI~/.config/dailydeck/config.toml\fR, created on first start).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Debug logging.
.TP
.B \-\-tray
Run with an icon in the top bar / notification area (quick settings, editor).
.TP
.B \-\-gui
Open the profile editor.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-focus
Print the identifiers of the focused window whenever they change.
.TP
.BI \-\-dry\-run " SHORTCUT"
Show which physical keys a shortcut would press, without pressing them.
.TP
.BI \-\-preview " DIR"
Render all profiles as PNG images into \fIDIR\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/dailydeck/config.toml
Profiles and settings; reloaded automatically when changed.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/60-dailydeck.rules
Access to the Stream Deck and /dev/uinput for the logged-in user.
.TP
.I /usr/share/gnome-shell/extensions/dailydeck-focus@thnow.github.io
GNOME Shell extension that reports the focused window on Wayland.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR udev (7)
